From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:25:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/37] [LLHD] RemoveControlFlow: lower joins by CFG structure,
 not per-edge path predicates

A join block's arguments were lowered as mux chains keyed by each incoming
edge's path predicate (an OR of AND-of-branch-conditions), so a value that
is identical along every arm of a nested `if` still depended structurally
on the branch conditions (v&~g | v&g&r | v&g&~r, a tautology in g that
canonicalize cannot fold). With g depending on that value elsewhere this
closed combinational loops the RTL does not have: ibex's 135-op
alu_operand_b -> stall_id -> lsu_req -> alu_op_b_mux_sel SCC, cv64a6's
miss-unit lock_reqs -> lzc -> FSM loop, store_buffer/wbuffer, icache.

StructuredJoin evaluates the dominator-to-join DAG forward: one mux per
cond_br on its own condition, arms folded when equal, successors that
cannot reach the join contribute no arm; drive enables use the same
structured reach condition. Gates: reproducer SCC 1 -> 0 + Yosys miter;
ibex SCC 1 -> 0 at every stage, flat core ops 7,071 -> 4,618, registers
identical, RTL-vs-core BMC from reset depth 6 SUCCESS; cv64a6 on a
regenerated raw 39 -> 0 SCCs; lit updated (+3 cases).

